# The Progression page (0.15.6): EDIT held opens it (a tap is still the next chord). Eight slots, each a chord of the scale (a degree, or none: the chord
# before holds) and its bars; Play Loop plays them in turn up to the last one set, Walk gives the chords back to the genre. The page shows the chords heard
# last until the first edit makes them the piece's. SEL + Drift: the chord's time in bars or in seconds, in any genre. Stored with the piece.
seed 0
wait 3000
press EDIT
wait 600
release EDIT
wait 100
expect view 5
expect progpos -1
expect prgplay 0
expect prgslot0 0
# the seeded piece is in A natural minor (pool 0x5AD): I is Am (root 9), VI F (5), IV Dm (2), V Em (4)
expect pool 0x5AD
shot progression_heard.png
# slot 1 (K1, Chord, at 1): I; slot 2 (a white key): VI; slot 3: IV; slot 4: V; eight bars each, so EDIT steps through them
turn K1 -8
turn K1 1
turn K3 4
expect prgplay 1
expect prgslot0 1
expect prgbars0 8
tapkey w1
turn K1 -8
turn K1 6
turn K3 4
tapkey w2
turn K1 -8
turn K1 4
turn K3 4
tapkey w3
turn K1 -8
turn K1 5
turn K3 4
expect prgslot1 6
expect prgslot2 4
expect prgslot3 5
expect prgbars3 8
wait 5000
expect progpos 0
expect chordroot 9
shot progression.png
tap EDIT
wait 2500
expect progpos 1
expect chordroot 5
tap EDIT
wait 2500
expect progpos 2
expect chordroot 2
tap EDIT
wait 2500
expect progpos 3
expect chordroot 4
shot progression_play.png
# the loop ends at the last slot set: then the first again
tap EDIT
wait 2500
expect progpos 0
expect chordroot 9
# an empty slot: the chord before goes on through it
tapkey w1
turn K1 -8
expect prgslot1 0
tap EDIT
wait 2500
expect progpos 1
expect chordroot 9
shot progression_hold.png
# a slot's own chord type (0.16.6, GitHub issue 2): slot 1's I (A minor) as an 11th, A G B D (the root, b7, 9, 11); the others keep the piece's
tapkey w0
turn K2 7
expect prgtype0 7
expect prgtype2 0
tap EDIT
wait 2500
tap EDIT
wait 2500
tap EDIT
wait 2500
expect progpos 0
expect chordiv 1061
shot progression_types.png
# Walk: the genre's chords again (the slots kept)
turn K4 -1
expect prgplay 0
expect progpos -1
expect prgslot2 4
turn K4 1
expect prgplay 1
# SEL + Drift on the Tempo page: hypno counts seconds, so right is bars (stored), left is its own seconds again (0)
turn SELECT -100 10
expect view 0
press SEL
turn K4 1
release SEL
expect prgunit 1
shot tempo_drift_bars.png
press SEL
turn K4 -1
release SEL
expect prgunit 0
# stored with the piece: Global, SAVE; power off and on
tap GLO
expect view 31
tap SAVE
wait 300
tap PLAY
wait 4000
reboot
wait 3000
expect prgslot0 1
expect prgslot2 4
expect prgplay 1
expect prgtype0 7
